*.md
.kilo/

# .lastmod.json is NOT ignored. It is the per-page content-hash ledger build.js
# uses to decide which <lastmod> dates advance, so it has to be committed with
# the site: without it in version history a fresh clone re-dates all 50 URLs on
# its first build and the sitemap once again claims the whole site is new.

# Deploy tooling. wrangler.jsonc and worker.js are part of the deployment and
# are committed; only the local cache it writes is not.
/.wrangler/
node_modules/

# .assetsignore is the file that stops wrangler uploading the working tree as
# public assets, so it must reach the build environment. Never ignore it.
!.assetsignore
